WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.426
When the queen traveled with the king, she liked to take Glumdalclitch and me with her.

2
00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:09.308
I enjoyed traveling with them and seeing the countryside.

3
00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:14.557
I was amazed at how big Brobdingnag was compared to England.

4
00:00:14.558 --> 00:00:17.687
"I can’t believe the size of your country!"

5
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:20.376
I often exclaimed to Glumdalclitch.

6
00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:25.686
"It is five thousand kilometers wide and ten thousand kilometers long.

7
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:29.042
England would fit into it many times over!

8
00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:33.926
I wonder why we in England have never heard of Brobdingnag."

9
00:00:33.927 --> 00:00:39.552
"The tutor said that my country is a peninsula," she reminded me.

10
00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:43.969
"That means that the sea surrounds the country on three sides.

11
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:51.559
On the fourth side, the mountains are so high that no one has ever been able to cross them.

12
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:56.962
The sea near Brobdingnag is full of rocks and always very rough.

13
00:00:56.963 --> 00:01:02.053
Before your ship, no other ship had ever come close to Brobdingnag.

14
00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:06.728
You are the first person from another country to come here."

15
00:01:06.729 --> 00:01:10.767
"My ship had almost run out of water," I told her.

16
00:01:10.768 --> 00:01:12.351
"We were desperate.

17
00:01:12.352 --> 00:01:16.058
That is why the sailors and I came here in the rowboat.

18
00:01:16.059 --> 00:01:19.596
We were lucky to find a little beach to land on."

19
00:01:19.597 --> 00:01:23.659
During our travels, I learned a lot about Brobdingnag.

20
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:29.880
It contained 51 big cities, hundreds of large towns, and many villages.

21
00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:32.147
We lived in the capital city.

22
00:01:32.148 --> 00:01:36.676
A river about five kilometers wide ran through the capital.

23
00:01:36.677 --> 00:01:43.258
The palace, which was near the river, was not just one building, but dozens of buildings.

24
00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:48.539
Even the smallest one was many times bigger than the largest building in England.

25
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.219
What really amazed me about the palace was the kitchen.

26
00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:55.236
Glumdalclitch and I visited it one day.

27
00:01:55.237 --> 00:02:01.354
"It looks to be almost two hundred meters high!" I exclaimed to Glumdalclitch.

28
00:02:01.355 --> 00:02:05.625
"And I’ve never seen pots and pans and knives this big. That

29
00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:09.280
knife there is three times as tall as I am! If

30
00:02:09.281 --> 00:02:15.863
I ever get back to England, no one will believe me when I tell them about this kitchen." My

31
00:02:15.864 --> 00:02:18.980
days in the capital were very pleasant. Sometimes

32
00:02:18.981 --> 00:02:21.760
Glumdalclitch said to me, "Let’s

33
00:02:21.761 --> 00:02:25.012
go out and explore the city. We

34
00:02:25.013 --> 00:02:28.095
always see such interesting things. Because

35
00:02:28.096 --> 00:02:34.041
I lived on a farm, I am just as curious as you are about this city." I

36
00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:37.445
enjoyed exploring, so I always said, "That’s

37
00:02:37.446 --> 00:02:39.636
a great idea." We

38
00:02:39.637 --> 00:02:44.306
traveled in one of the palace carriages pulled by horses. Glumdalclitch

39
00:02:44.307 --> 00:02:48.564
put me in my box and held it on her lap. "Look

40
00:02:48.565 --> 00:02:53.444
at that," she would say to me when something caught her attention. "Would

41
00:02:53.445 --> 00:02:55.642
you like a better view? I’ll

42
00:02:55.643 --> 00:03:00.124
ask the driver to stop so that you can see better." One

43
00:03:00.125 --> 00:03:06.037
day the queen said, "Your bedroom box is too big for traveling. Glumdalclitch

44
00:03:06.038 --> 00:03:12.828
has trouble holding it on her lap, and I am afraid that she might drop it. I

45
00:03:12.829 --> 00:03:17.098
will tell the carpenter to make you a smaller one." "How

46
00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:20.558
kind of you," I said to her. "A

47
00:03:20.559 --> 00:03:23.800
smaller box will be much more convenient." My

48
00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:30.378
new traveling box was about three and a half meters square and three meters high. Three

49
00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:35.395
of the walls had a window with metal bars on the outside to protect me. Two

50
00:03:35.396 --> 00:03:43.254
large loops on the fourth side of my box could be used to tie the box to the waist of whoever carried it. "Look!"

51
00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:46.413
exclaimed Glumdalclitch. "The

52
00:03:46.414 --> 00:03:49.569
furniture is attached to the floor. It

53
00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.432
can’t move around and hurt you!" Also,

54
00:03:52.433 --> 00:03:56.437
the clever carpenter had hung a hammock from the ceiling. "Are

55
00:03:56.438 --> 00:04:00.957
you comfortable?" she asked as she carried my box. "

56
00:04:00.958 --> 00:04:09.099
Very comfortable," I replied, swinging in my cozy hammock.

